			<div class="content" id="post-content-1419286">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Any persons entering or exiting SCP-1165 are to be detained, debriefed, and administered a Class-B amnesiac.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This should say &quot;Any unauthorized persons&quot; (or something similar) to make it clear that survey team aren't regularly having their memories wiped upon returning.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Cellular phones and GPS devices continue to function within SCP-1165 and indicate that the device is in a location relative to the distance the bearer has traveled from the western exit of the alley.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So radio waves can travel into and out of the SCP?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Discovering the area to be abandoned, they had taken to squatting in a residential building and scavenging food and alcohol from a building resembling a convenience store.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This suggests that there isn't any food to be found in any of the residential buildings.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Food was found to be fresh and edible,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Hmmm, if I was the Foundation I'd leave behind some surveillance equipment to see if the food was being restocked.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>During a survey of the area near the first apparent location of the ██████ █████, a sudden power outage resulted in the loss of cell phone service within the ███████ area.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why are Foundation exploratory teams using cell phones to remain in contact with mission control? Even if they're cheap, it doesn't seem like a very secure way of communicating.</p>
<p>Also, I found the redactions in the survey log to be frustrating rather than suggestive.</p>

